Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:08:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept a message in fewer database round trips
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 9 (16 Oct, 200 „გამარჯობა" at once): outside the load every accept
phase was a multiple of ~150 ms, one round trip to the database each, and
under the load each trip grew to 0.5-1 s with no pool waiting and no loop
lag. Two waits depended on nothing:

- the provisional title waited for the thread and the wallet check waited
  for the title; the title is now written beside the wallet check and
  awaited before the 402 or the 202, so a reply never goes before it;
- the wallet check read the subscription only after the grant expiry; it is
  now read beside it. The grant still comes after the expiry, which reads
  the balance the grant would change.

About 0.45 s off every accepted message with nobody else on the server, and
the same two trips' share under load. No text or behaviour changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
